; frame: 256 B locals + 256 B peak string temps = 512 B
; [110] 
; [111] { ---- Variables -----------------------------------------------------------
; [112] 
; [113]   0 = stack, 1..15 = local, 16..255 = global.
; [114] 
; [115]   EVERY local index goes through ZLIdx and lands in a plain variable before
; [116]   it is used. This is not style. It works around a compiler bug found here
; [117]   in Part 26 and FIXED in the same part -- kept because it costs nothing and
; [118]   the reasoning is worth preserving.
; [119] 
; [120]   The trigger was a PROCEDURE PARAMETER used as an array index on the left
; [121]   of `:=', compound or not. `A[v] := 1234' was enough:
; [122] 
; [123]       A[v] := 1234        <-- assigned 1234 to v
; [124]       idx := v;
; [125]       A[idx] := 1234;     <-- correct
; [126] 
; [127]   It did not fail to store. It stored into the PARAMETER'S OWN FRAME SLOT.
; [128]   EmitAddress set DestIsXY2 on the first frame access while parsing the LHS
; [129]   -- for a subscripted destination that is the INDEX -- so EmitStore took
; [130]   its [XY2+#N] fast path with the index's offset. The element address was
; [131]   computed correctly in D0 and thrown away.
; [132] 
; [133]   READS through the identical index were fine, which is what made it so slow
; [134]   to find: locals returned their header initial values forever while every
; [135]   write vanished, and Zork's serial-number loop span with its output
; [136]   swallowed by the wrap buffer. `base + i' stored correctly because both are
; [137]   var-section locals, which this compiler allocates statically and addresses
; [138]   by page, not by frame -- so ZDoCall worked and the fault looked like a read
; [139]   problem somewhere else entirely.
; [140] 
; [141]   Reduced in bug.pas / zvartest.pas / zidxtest2.pas; fixed by DestXY2Mark in
; [142]   K16Pascal_codegen.inc plus the validation in ParseAssignment.
; [143]   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- }
; [144] 
; [145] { Flat index of local n (1..15) in the current frame.
; [146] 
; [147]   An add, not a multiply -- see ZFBase in zstate.pas. Kept as a function for
; [148]   the indirect forms below, which are rare; the two hot accessors inline it,
; [149]   because on this path a CALL16/RET costs more than the arithmetic does. }
; [150] function ZLIdx(v: Word): Word;
